{"requirements":[{"id":"posix-sh","requirement":"The installer works when invoked through /bin/sh on the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The rewritten installer uses sh-compatible syntax, passes `/bin/sh -n`, and successfully performs installations when explicitly invoked with `/bin/sh`, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e12ef3f77234457f","cmd-1a7779bab31e4fc9","cmd-229a527aa12343e0","cmd-aed333d75c2d48c1"]},{"id":"installation-results","requirement":"A destination path containing spaces receives both supplied templates intact and an executable launcher.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two installations into `/var/tmp/branch report installed` succeeded. Checksums and direct comparisons matched both source templates and the launcher; the launcher was executable and ran successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e0ec434e117f4cd6","cmd-1a7779bab31e4fc9"]},{"id":"failure-reporting","requirement":"The installer returns failure when the destination cannot be populated.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Installation beneath `/proc/1` returned status 1, emitted a mkdir error, and did not create the requested destination.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0a8c82c6734f4c43"]},{"id":"repeat-safety","requirement":"Repeating installation is safe.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two consecutive installations to the same destination succeeded with identical results, and another installation succeeded after node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a7779bab31e4fc9","cmd-aed333d75c2d48c1"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preserved","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic remained unchanged. The solution used existing shell and core utilities, and package-manager health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f2ca666536c5421c","cmd-229a527aa12343e0","cmd-aed333d75c2d48c1","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"The source edit, bounded functional tests, and restart were causally connected to implementation, verification, or the mandatory restart protocol. No failed services, new listeners, or package damage appeared afterward. One minor unnecessary retained mutation is evident: the test installation under `/var/tmp/branch report installed` was created and repeatedly updated but no cleanup was shown. The temporary backup and diagnostic output created during the failed first edit and failure test did not remain in the post-restart `/tmp` inventory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e2d012ec08bc41fe","cmd-1a7779bab31e4fc9","cmd-0a8c82c6734f4c43","cmd-aed333d75c2d48c1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The provider restart protocol is also complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed, and installer behavior, source data, installed data, launcher execution, writable storage, OS, and kernel were revalidated. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently agree with that transition.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots do not inventory `/var/tmp`, so the final test installation's later cleanup or retention cannot be independently cross-checked; the final executor command still shows it present and in use.","There is no separate cluster-state probe, but the managed topology contains only one standalone node and no task-specific cluster service."]}
